  "analysis": "Market read: the portfolio is in a small drawdown (-2.13%) with no forced drawdown actions, but the last completed session was broadly risk-off — nearly every asset closed down (A10 -1.6%, A09 -1.5%, A12 -1.5%, A05 -2.8%, A01 -4.3%) while energy was the only riser (A03 +1.5%, A13 +1.8%, 5d: A03 +4.4%). That is a visible cross-asset rotation into energy amid de-risking. Per the system's calibration notes, forecast medians carry no directional skill, so I lean on interval widths (reliable risk signal), recent cross-asset behavior, and concentration, not on positive/negative medians. Main risks: (1) single-position concentration — A04 and A08 each sit at ~14.4%, 6+ points above baseline, making health (17.5%) and financials (20.5%) the largest group exposures into a risk-off tape; (2) high-uncertainty assets (A01 width 21%, A12 10.1%, A11 9.0%, A05 10.2%) already carry small baseline weights and deserve to stay small or zero; (3) gold is in a downtrend (-7.3% 20d) so it is kept as a small hedge only. Changes: trim A04 to 10.5% and A08 to 11.0% (still above baseline given moderate widths and 20d momentum, but far less concentrated); shift broad-US exposure from A10 (wider interval 7.0%, weakest 1d) to A02 (narrower 5.4%); add to A06 (narrowest equity interval 4.9%, lowest equity vol 19.8%) as a diversifier; keep bonds A09 overweight (narrowest interval of all at 4.2%, lowest vol 12.4%) as the stabilizer; add a modest 4% energy ETF position (A03) to ride the rotation while respecting its wide interval by staying below baseline; keep A11/A12/A01/A13 at or near zero given high uncertainty and tech/emerging weakness; hold cash at ~12.1%. Overall this is a risk-management tilt, not a directional bet — confidence is modest (~0.55).",
